    "body": "Fixes #7921.\r\n\r\nThe issue was that the tuple elements were cleaned up in generate_evaluation_code, so it worked for simple tuple elements (i.e. literals or names) but not for more complex ones that were evaluated into a temp.\r\n\r\nTo fix this pass PyMethodCallNode both the array of kwnames, and the tuple containing them. Non-literal elements are passed as `CloneNode` into the tuple\r\n(ensuring that they're only evaluated once). Literal elements are just copied so literal kwnames tuples can be reproduced as before.",
    "closed_at": null,
